@prefix orexis: <http://example.org/orexis#> .
@prefix journal: <http://example.org/orexis/journal#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix owl:  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix : <http://example.org/orexis/journal#> .

<> a orexis:OntologyGraph .    # this document is one graph, and this is what it is

#  OREXIS JOURNAL.
#  THE JOURNAL PACKAGE'S OWN WORD: the role it is loaded for. What an entry of the journal is said in — an event
#  beneath `orexis:Event`, an incident beneath `orexis:Incident`, a log record, an activity's seconds — stays the
#  kernel's, since every package's events are declared beneath those and the journal's readers ask by them.

#  THE ROLE THIS PACKAGE SERVES (knowledge/domain/journal/recorder.md): an agent declared a recorder keeps a journal,
#  and the boot loads this package for it and for nothing else. An agent declared none says what happens as any
#  other does, and nobody writes it down.

journal:Recorder a owl:Class ; rdfs:subClassOf orexis:Role ; rdfs:label "Recorder" ;
    rdfs:comment "An agent that keeps a journal of what happened to it: every event its packages say and every activity they end, written as it happens. Declared, never derived; it changes nothing the agent plans or does." .

#  WHAT A RECORDER'S ROLE IS LINKED TO decides which of the two crates that keep house for the journal join it: the
#  role names a tracer, and what ships the activities joins; it names an archive, and what takes the lasting entries
#  to disk joins; it names neither, and the journal is kept in memory for its window and nothing else is run. The
#  role says WHICH service, and the world's deployment graph (`orexis:DeploymentGraph`) WHERE it answers.

#  WHERE THE ACTIVITIES ARE SHIPPED (knowledge/domain/journal/tracer.md).

journal:Tracer a owl:Class ; rdfs:label "Tracer" ;
    rdfs:comment "A service the world is connected to that takes an agent's activities as spans, OTLP over HTTP at its `schema:url`, which the world's deployment graph (`orexis:DeploymentGraph`) states. What ships the journal's activities (`orexis-journal-otlp/`) finds it there as it starts, by the recorder's role that names it." .

journal:tracedBy a owl:ObjectProperty ; rdfs:label "traced by" ;
    rdfs:domain journal:Recorder ; rdfs:range journal:Tracer ;
    rdfs:comment "The tracer a recorder's activities are shipped to, said of the role in the agent's self graph. A recorder whose role names none is traced by nobody, and what ships the activities ends its start." .

#  WHERE WHAT LASTS IS KEPT (knowledge/domain/journal/archive.md).

journal:Archive a owl:Class ; rdfs:label "Archive" ;
    rdfs:comment "A triplestore on a volume of the agent's own holding what its journal kept for good, at the `file:` url the world's deployment graph (`orexis:DeploymentGraph`) states as its `schema:url`. What archives the journal (`orexis-journal-oxigraph/`) finds it there as it starts, by the recorder's role that names it." .

journal:archivedIn a owl:ObjectProperty ; rdfs:label "archived in" ;
    rdfs:domain journal:Recorder ; rdfs:range journal:Archive ;
    rdfs:comment "The archive what a recorder's journal keeps for good is taken to, said of the role in the agent's self graph. A recorder whose role names none has no archive: what lasts stays in its journal, in memory." .
